---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SplitSection from "../components/SplitSection.astro";
import AboutIntro from "../components/AboutIntro.astro";
import Appearances from "../components/Appearances.astro";
---

<Base title="About Niko Karppinen" description="Niko Karppinen is an SEO and analytics consultant working across digital measurement, technical implementation and practical digital systems." schemaPageType="about">
  <AboutIntro />

  <SplitSection id="approach" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>How I approach work</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        Good systems should make the next decision easier. That is usually the
        test I come back to, whether I am working on measurement, site structure,
        tracking, or something in between.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work often sits between SEO, analytics, content, tracking, and technical
        implementation. I look at how those areas connect rather than treating
        each one as a separate problem. Sometimes that also means questioning the
        problem itself. Are we solving the right thing, or have we simply accepted
        the original framing?
      </p>
      <p>
        When something feels abstract, I try to make it concrete. That might mean
        using examples, analogies, diagrams, or a small working model. I would
        rather build something that can be tested than leave behind a vague
        recommendation that sounds finished.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI can help apply a clear process more consistently. It does not fix bad
        source data, unclear ownership, or a process that nobody really
        understands.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <SplitSection id="values" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>What I care about</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        I care about clarity, trust, and useful structure. Measurement should
        support real decisions, not produce more numbers to maintain.
      </p>
      <p>
        Good work should give people enough context to judge what matters and
        enough structure to act on it. Tools can surface patterns, but people
        still decide what matters for the customer, the business, and the brand.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <SplitSection id="background" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>Background</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        I have worked with SEO, analytics, and digital marketing since 2017.
        During that time, I have worked with organisations in ecommerce,
        telecommunications, insurance, healthcare, the public sector, B2B, and
        consumer services.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work has covered technical SEO, analytics and tracking implementations,
        consent setups, measurement planning, dashboards, website redesigns, and
        search-driven site structure planning.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have always been interested in how technology, content, structure,
        and storytelling fit together. I have written short-film screenplays too.
        Not as a professional credential, but because I enjoy figuring out how
        ideas, pacing, and communication work together.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <SplitSection id="outside-work" variant="about">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      <h2>Outside work</h2>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="copy">
      <p>
        Outside work, I spend a lot of time with films, anime, and
        story-driven single-player games. Alan Wake and Metal Gear Solid are
        particular favourites. I tend to like stories with strong structure,
        atmosphere, and worlds that are a little strange.
      </p>
      <p>
        Comics are another constant, especially Batman and Teenage Mutant Ninja
        Turtles. I have a soft spot for strong concepts and worlds that take
        their own internal logic seriously.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also dance Cuban salsa and locking. Both involve structure, rhythm,
        practice, and improvisation. They are also very efficient at exposing
        misplaced confidence.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </SplitSection>

  <Appearances />
</Base>
